src/lib/ecs-js/README.md:158:Resources are runtime-only by default. A resource appears in snapshots only when its definition opts in with `serializable: true` and the caller explicitly names that resource during capture, for example `serializeWorld(world, { includeResources: trapStepQueue })`. Restoring that resource requires the target world to already know the definition or for `applySnapshot(..., { resources: [...] })` to receive it. Prefer singleton components for durable simulation facts that should be queried, saved, and inspected as part of the world model.

